#Дизайн_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Человек в Work Graph является оператором и reviewer: он наблюдает за задачами, evidence, worker runs и memory updates, но не рисует граф вручную.
  Текущий backlog board уже показывает Work Graph snapshot v1; operator dashboard расширяет его до операционного экрана проекта, не заменяя runtime, evidence или memory contracts.
  Source of truth остаётся .bvc Work Graph; dashboard читает derived snapshot, runner log/evidence projection и memory summary.
Вектор:
  Главный экран показывает current task/next action, ready queue, in_progress runs, blocked tasks, verify queue, последние Evidence v1 records, Worker Output summaries и Project Memory update candidates.
  Board/backlog остаётся основной очередью задач: колонки ready, in_progress, verify, blocked, done и отдельный backlog view, с группировкой по department, owner role, priority and risk.
  Blocked lane поднимается в отдельный операторский фокус: blocker reason, next unblock action, last failed worker run, related evidence and owner role.
  Evidence feed показывает command/test/file/change/decision/worker-run/manual-review/blocker records с status, source, summary, artifacts, command/exitCode, provider and runId where available.
  Worker/provider run status показывает provider id/type, runId, started/finished time, status, retry advice, logs/artifacts, transitionRequest and cancellation state without relying on hidden provider session state.
  Memory panel показывает draft/needs-review/active Project Memory records created from done tasks, worker output, verification results, blocker resolution and explicit human decisions.
Цель:
  Оператор понимает, что делает агент, почему задача может двигаться дальше, где нужен человек, и может вмешаться через policy-gated controls без raw .bvc editing или manual graph editor.

Проверки:
  dashboard не требует ручного рисования графа
  есть список intervention controls
  MVP отделён от later scope
  dashboard использует Work Graph snapshot, Evidence v1, Project Memory v1 and Worker Output
  manual graph editor явно указан как non-goal

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  design.id: operator-dashboard
  design.input: workgraph.snapshot.v1
  design.input: evidence-record-v1
  design.input: memory-record-v1
  design.input: agent-worker-output-v1
  design.next_work: design-operator-dashboard-snapshot
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Scope_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Operator dashboard должен объединить уже описанные контракты в один пользовательский экран, а не открыть новую реализацию scheduler-а или memory store.
Вектор:
  Scope includes: current/next task visibility, backlog/board, blocked task focus, evidence feed, worker/provider run status, memory updates, intervention controls, readonly derived graph entry point and task detail drawer.
  Current task card shows WorkItem id/title/status, basis/vector/goal summary, nextAction, DoD/checks, dependencies, target files, trace status and latest evidence gate state.
  Queue view shows ready and verify candidates from snapshot readyQueue/statusCounts, with dependency satisfaction and risk/priority indicators.
  Detail drawer is the primary drilldown: WorkItem BVC, dependencies, checks, target files, evidence records, worker runs, memory candidates and allowed actions.
  Readonly graph viewer is a later linked surface derived from Work Graph edges/evidence/file refs; dashboard may open it focused on a task but does not author nodes or edges.
Цель:
  The artifact defines product/design scope for the operator surface before adding a dashboard-specific snapshot or broad UI implementation.

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  design.section: operator-dashboard-scope
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  MVP must be useful on top of existing Work Graph runtime, backlog UI server and local runner contracts.
Вектор:
  MVP includes: status summary, active task/current run card, board/backlog, blocked tasks panel, recent evidence feed, task detail drawer, and read-only display of worker output and memory update candidates.
  MVP sidebar views include board, backlog, architecture L1 map, schematic Work Graph OS loop, task dependency graph, verification loop panel and later memory; schematic is readonly derived SVG without manual graph editor.
  MVP actions are policy-gated and may start as runtime/API contracts before full UI forms: claim, block, unblock, record evidence, open detail drawer, request provider/local runner run and stop/cancel run.
  MVP uses polling of a dashboard snapshot derived from Work Graph snapshot plus runner/evidence/memory projections; it does not require websocket/event streaming.
  MVP records every state-changing action as Evidence v1 or Work Graph transition evidence; done/verify gates remain enforced by runtime, not by client UI.
  MVP graph support is an "open readonly graph/detail" affordance, not a graph editing canvas.
Цель:
  Ship one operational dashboard that explains the current agent loop and supports safe human intervention.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: operator-dashboard-mvp-scope
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Later_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Several useful operator conveniences require stronger runner logs, memory writer and dashboard snapshot contracts.
Вектор:
  Later includes: full readonly derived graph viewer, richer auto-layout graph exploration, provider registry/cost/token views, retry schedule visualization, notifications, Telegram/tray/mobile channels, websocket/event streaming and advanced memory review workflows.
  Later includes batch operations only after runtime policy can validate each transition and evidence record independently.
  Later may add SQLite/NDJSON/GBC-derived caches for runner logs or dashboard speed, but not as canonical task state.
  Later may add domain-specific panels such as OneBase artifact trace after language/domain adapters expose structured facts.
Цель:
  Keep MVP focused on Work Graph operations while preserving a path to richer project operating system views.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: operator-dashboard-later-scope
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Data_Boundaries_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Dashboard must not parse raw .bvc or provider transcripts to infer core state.
Вектор:
  Work Graph snapshot v1 supplies schema, source, items, edges, statusCounts and readyQueue; item fields supply task card and board/backlog state.
  Evidence v1 supplies structured feed records: id, time, source, taskId, type, summary, status, details, artifacts, command, exitCode, provider and runId.
  Worker Output v1 supplies run result: runId, taskId, status, patchSummary, evidence, transitionRequest, logs, failureReason and retryAdvice; runtime normalizes it into evidence and transition proposals.
  Project Memory v1 supplies bounded memory summaries and candidate records: id, type, summary, sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds, confidence, status, updatedAt, relatedFiles and relatedTasks.
  Dashboard-specific snapshot is a derived join of these projections; it contains display-ready currentTask, queues, blockers, recentEvidence, runnerStatus, memoryUpdates and actionFeed, but no independent scheduler state.
Цель:
  UI can explain work, proof, runs and memory without owning canonical state or replaying hidden sessions.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: operator-dashboard-data-boundaries
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Intervention_Controls<[
Базис:
  Operator controls should be narrow, auditable and consistent with Work Graph runtime policy.
Вектор:
  claim: assign/claim a ready task; runtime checks dependencies and current status before moving it to in_progress/claimed.
  block: record blocker reason, next unblock action and blocker evidence; runtime moves task to blocked only with reason/evidence.
  unblock: clear blocker by recording resolution evidence and moving task to ready or in_progress according to policy.
  record evidence: create Evidence v1 record for command/test/file/change/decision/manual-review/blocker and attach it to the task.
  open detail drawer: inspect BVC, labels, checks, evidence, target files, worker runs, memory candidates and allowed actions for one WorkItem.
  request provider run: ask runtime/scheduler to build Worker Input from current snapshot, memory slice, target files and policy, then start local or provider adapter.
  stop/cancel run: request cancellation for a runId; adapter returns cancelled Worker Output with partial evidence/logs and no implicit done transition.
Цель:
  Human intervention is recorded as Work Graph/evidence events instead of out-of-band edits or opaque provider messages.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: operator-dashboard-intervention-controls
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Non_Goals_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  The dashboard must not repeat the previous heavy visual editor path.
Вектор:
  Non-goal: manual graph editor, manual node/edge drawing, freeform React Flow-like editing or making visual layout the source of truth.
  Non-goal: direct raw .bvc editing as the primary operator interaction; atom inspector/forms can be opened later through structured StepAtomDraft.
  Non-goal: provider-specific session browser; logs/transcripts are artifacts, while dashboard state comes from Worker Output and Evidence v1.
  Non-goal: memory vault UI as canonical state; memory records remain Project Memory v1 with derived human-readable projections.
  Non-goal: queue database as task source of truth; runner queues/logs are derived execution projections around Work Graph.
Цель:
  Keep the operator surface focused on observable project operations, evidence and review.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: operator-dashboard-non-goals
  trace.status: verified
]>
#Дизайн_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Человек в Work Graph является оператором, reviewer и policy owner, а не ручным автором графа.
  Текущий backlog board уже показывает WorkItem статусы из workgraph.snapshot.v1; operator dashboard расширяет этот экран до операционной панели агента.
  Dashboard читает derived snapshot/evidence/memory/runner projections и не парсит raw .bvc в браузере.
Вектор:
  Основной экран показывает current/next task, board/backlog, blocked tasks, recent evidence feed, worker/provider run status, pending memory updates and intervention controls.
  Work Graph snapshot остаётся базовым входом для задач, dependencies, статусов, target files, DoD/checks and trace status.
  Evidence v1 даёт ленту proof: command/test/change/file/decision/worker-run/manual-review/blocker records with status, artifacts, provider and runId.
  Project Memory v1 даёт компактные memory updates: новые или изменённые decision/invariant/risk/open-question/evidence-summary records with sourceWorkItem and evidenceIds.
  Worker Output v1 даёт run summary: provider, runId, status, patchSummary, logs/artifacts, failureReason, retryAdvice and transitionRequest.
Цель:
  Оператор понимает, что агент делает сейчас, что должно идти дальше, где блокеры, какие evidence/memory появились, и может вмешаться через policy-gated controls без ручной правки .bvc или ручного рисования графа.

Проверки:
  dashboard не требует ручного рисования графа
  есть список intervention controls
  выбран готовый graph viewer подход
  explicit non-goal: manual graph editor

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  design.id: operator-dashboard
  design.input: workgraph.snapshot.v1, evidence-record-v1, memory-record-v1, worker-output-v1
  design.scope: operator-dashboard
  work.source: design-operator-dashboard
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Scope_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Backlog board является первым UI, но оператору нужна картина execution loop: task -> worker run -> evidence -> memory -> next action.
Вектор:
  Header: active project, snapshot time/source, selected provider/runner mode, last successful verification and global health.
  Current task panel: claimed/in_progress/verify task with title, owner role, department, priority/risk, target files, DoD/checks, nextAction and dependency context.
  Next task panel: top readyQueue candidate and why it is claimable; show blocked dependency reason when no next task exists.
  Board/backlog: reuse backlog board columns ready, in_progress, verify, blocked, done and a backlog planning tab; keep grouping by department, ownerRole, priority and risk.
  Blockers panel: blocked WorkItems and failed/blocked evidence with reason, next unblock action, owner role and affected files.
  Evidence feed: recent Evidence v1 records grouped by task/run with filters for failed, blocked, test, worker-run and manual-review.
  Worker/provider status: active run, queued runnable projections, provider id/type, elapsed time, timeout, retry count, cost/tokens if available, cancellation state, logs/artifacts and transition proposal.
  Memory updates: draft/needs-review Project Memory candidates and active updates produced from successful evidence, with sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds and related files/tasks.
  Detail drawer: WorkItem inspector showing BVC, labels, checks, evidence, target files, Worker Output summary and memory links; form editing belongs to the later atom inspector task.
Цель:
  Dashboard is an operating surface for observing and steering the project loop, not a separate task database or provider session UI.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  design.id: operator-dashboard-scope
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Vs_Later<[
Базис:
  MVP must ship a useful design boundary without expanding into a broad UI implementation.
Вектор:
  MVP includes: current task, next task, board/backlog, blockers, recent evidence feed, worker/provider run summary, memory update summary, detail drawer and minimal intervention controls.
  MVP uses polling over a derived dashboard snapshot; no browser raw .bvc parsing and no independent scheduler state.
  MVP graph view is readonly and derived: show dependency/evidence/file/memory relationships through a ready-made renderer approach, with layout generated from snapshot edges and artifact links.
  Later includes: durable runner queue UI, provider registry management, cost dashboard, notifications, scheduling calendar, memory review inbox workflows, atom inspector form editing, richer graph filters and external integrations.
  Later graph renderer recommendation: start with Mermaid or Graphviz for static dependency/evidence diagrams; move to Cytoscape.js + Dagre/ELK only when interactive focus/expand/collapse is needed.
Цель:
  MVP explains and controls the loop; later work adds deeper management surfaces once snapshot, runner and memory contracts are implemented.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: operator-dashboard-mvp-later
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Input_Contracts<[
Базис:
  Operator dashboard must compose existing contracts instead of inventing a new source of truth.
Вектор:
  Work Graph snapshot v1 provides schema, source, items, edges, statusCounts and readyQueue; item fields provide id, title, status, ownerRole, department, priority, risk, dependsOn, targetFiles, traceStatus, nextAction, evidence, checks and blocker.
  Evidence v1 provides structured records with id, time, source, taskId, type, summary, status, artifacts, command, exitCode, provider and runId.
  Project Memory v1 provides MemoryRecord updates with id, type, summary, sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds, confidence, status, updatedAt, relatedFiles and relatedTasks.
  Worker Output v1 provides runId, taskId, status, patchSummary, evidence, transitionRequest, logs, failureReason and retryAdvice.
  PromptPilot runner patterns are adapted only as derived runner records: provider, duration, retry/rate-limit state, logs, artifacts and proposed transition; queue/cache is not canonical task state.
  Claude Note memory patterns are adapted only as extraction/update summaries; transcript dumps and provider-specific note stores are not dashboard state.
Цель:
  Every dashboard field can be rebuilt from Work Graph, Evidence, Project Memory and runner output projections.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: operator-dashboard-input-contracts
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Intervention_Controls<[
Базис:
  Operator controls should call Work Graph runtime or runner policy endpoints, not mutate browser state as truth.
Вектор:
  Claim: claim the top ready task or a selected ready task through runtime policy.
  Block: set blocked with blocker reason and blocker evidence; require next unblock action.
  Unblock: remove/resolve blocker by creating resolution evidence and returning the task to ready or verify by policy.
  Record evidence: add Evidence v1 command/test/file/change/decision/manual-review/blocker record with required fields and artifact refs.
  Open detail drawer: inspect WorkItem BVC, labels, checks, target files, evidence, Worker Output, memory updates and trace refs.
  Request provider run: create a runnable projection from current Work Graph snapshot, selected provider capability and allowed policy; runtime builds Worker Input v1 at execution time.
  Stop/cancel run: request cancellation for an active run; resulting Worker Output status=cancelled is recorded as evidence and does not silently mark done.
  Retry or switch provider: later control after failure evidence exists; retry starts from fresh snapshot and prior evidence/log summaries, not hidden provider session state.
Цель:
  Controls let the human steer execution while status transitions remain evidence-gated and reproducible.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: operator-dashboard-intervention-controls
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Non_Goals_Operator_Dashboard<[
Базис:
  Without non-goals the dashboard can drift into an expensive visual editor or provider console.
Вектор:
  Do not build a manual graph editor; graph nodes and edges are derived from WorkItems, dependencies, evidence, target files and memory links.
  Do not make the UI, runner queue, provider session, transcript or memory notes the source of truth; .bvc Work Graph plus structured evidence/memory artifacts remain canonical.
  Do not add broad React Flow-like editing, drag-to-create dependency state or freeform task DB mutations in MVP.
  Do not implement the atom inspector form inside this design task; the drawer can inspect and later link to design-atom-inspector-form.
  Do not build a Claude-only, Cursor-only or PromptPilot-only dashboard; provider details are adapter/run metadata behind Worker Output and Evidence v1.
Цель:
  Dashboard stays focused on operating and reviewing the Work Graph loop.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: operator-dashboard-non-goals
  trace.status: verified
]>
